# Tests for the Educator_adjustment module (issue #24)

Run with `clerk test`. Hand-worked TY2024 cases from the Form 1040
instructions, Schedule 1 line 11 (`i1040gi--2024.pdf` p 89): "up to $300 ...
If you and your spouse are filing jointly and both of you were eligible
educators, the maximum deduction is $600. However, neither spouse can deduct
more than $300". The oracle comparison is
`make difftest SCOPE=educator_adjustment`.

> Using Educator_adjustment as E

## Wrapper with defaults

A wrapper scope gives every input a default (not an educator, $0 expenses,
not an MFJ dependent) so each test states only what it changes. The defaults
are satisfiable: they are an ordinary taxpayer who is not an educator.

```catala
declaration scope Base:
  context was_k12_educators content E.K12EducatorOptions
  context primary_expenses content money
  context secondary_expenses content money
  context is_mfj_dependent condition
  e scope E.EducatorAdjustment
  output adjustment content money
  output receiving condition

scope Base:
  definition was_k12_educators equals Neither
  definition primary_expenses equals $0
  definition secondary_expenses equals $0
  definition is_mfj_dependent equals false
  definition e.was_k12_educators equals was_k12_educators
  definition e.primary_educator_expenses_writable equals primary_expenses
  definition e.secondary_educator_expenses_writable equals secondary_expenses
  definition e.is_mfj_dependent equals is_mfj_dependent
  definition adjustment equals e.educator_expenses_adjustment
  definition receiving equals e.is_receiving_educator_expenses_adjustment
```

## Acceptance cases

A single educator with $450 of expenses gets the $300 cap; one with $175 gets
$175; an MFJ couple who both taught, each with $450, get $600; with $12 and
$250 (oracle `mfj-44k`) they get $262.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestEducatorCases:
  output ok condition
  single_450 scope Base
  single_175 scope Base
  both_450 scope Base
  both_12_250 scope Base
  boundary_300 scope Base
  spouse_only scope Base

scope TestEducatorCases:
  rule ok fulfilled
  definition single_450.was_k12_educators equals TpDid
  definition single_450.primary_expenses equals $450
  definition single_175.was_k12_educators equals TpDid
  definition single_175.primary_expenses equals $175
  definition both_450.was_k12_educators equals BothDid
  definition both_450.primary_expenses equals $450
  definition both_450.secondary_expenses equals $450
  definition both_12_250.was_k12_educators equals BothDid
  definition both_12_250.primary_expenses equals $12
  definition both_12_250.secondary_expenses equals $250
  definition boundary_300.was_k12_educators equals TpDid
  definition boundary_300.primary_expenses equals $300
  definition spouse_only.was_k12_educators equals SpouseDid
  definition spouse_only.primary_expenses equals $999
  definition spouse_only.secondary_expenses equals $208
  assertion single_450.adjustment = $300
  assertion single_175.adjustment = $175
  assertion both_450.adjustment = $600
  assertion both_12_250.adjustment = $262
  assertion boundary_300.adjustment = $300
  # the spouse's $999 is ignored when only the spouse is the educator
  assertion spouse_only.adjustment = $208
```

## Zero cases

Not an educator: expenses entered in the writable boxes are ignored (DF
`/primaryEducatorExpenses` is `$0` unless `/tpWasK12Educator`). An MFJ
dependent gets `$0` (DF `/educatorExpensesAdjustment`).

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestEducatorZero:
  output ok condition
  neither scope Base
  dependent scope Base

scope TestEducatorZero:
  rule ok fulfilled
  definition neither.was_k12_educators equals Neither
  definition neither.primary_expenses equals $300
  definition neither.secondary_expenses equals $300
  definition dependent.was_k12_educators equals BothDid
  definition dependent.primary_expenses equals $300
  definition dependent.secondary_expenses equals $300
  definition dependent.is_mfj_dependent equals true
  assertion neither.adjustment = $0
  assertion dependent.adjustment = $0
  assertion not neither.receiving
  assertion not dependent.receiving
```

## The spec rejects bad outputs

A $450 single educator must not get $450 (cap ignored) and an MFJ couple must
not get more than $600; the specification gives exactly $300 and $600, so any
other value is rejected.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestEducatorRejectsBad:
  output ok condition
  single_450 scope Base
  both_450 scope Base

scope TestEducatorRejectsBad:
  rule ok fulfilled
  definition single_450.was_k12_educators equals TpDid
  definition single_450.primary_expenses equals $450
  definition both_450.was_k12_educators equals BothDid
  definition both_450.primary_expenses equals $450
  definition both_450.secondary_expenses equals $450
  assertion not (single_450.adjustment = $450)
  assertion not (single_450.adjustment = $0)
  assertion not (both_450.adjustment = $900)
  assertion not (both_450.adjustment = $300)
```
